From 3282aa2a47b6d1b362631ae824cadf702cf2d68b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:56:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: re-add a worktree card's deleted working
 copy from its branch instead of giving up (self-heal kanban-9101461fb6)

A worktree card t_0000000000000001 (worktree ~/code/sample-dev/task-1175, branch sample-dev/task-1175,
repo ~/code/sample-dev/myapp) woke after its tree was removed. _resolve_worktree_workspace found no repo
above the sibling-layout path and raised WorktreeWorkspaceConfigError ('use workspace_path=<repo root>'),
so the dispatcher sticky-blocked a valid card although its branch still existed.

When a concrete worktree path is gone and the card's branch_name exists in exactly one repo next to it
(a main checkout or a sibling linked worktree's common dir) or in the board default_workdir, prune and
re-add it on that branch (never creates a branch) and log a worktree_restored event (path, repo, branch,
restored_at) so the next deletion can be matched against cleanup logs. If no repo has the branch, the
error says the working copy was deleted after the card ran, not 'use workspace_path=<repo root>'.

Test: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_worktree_restore.py (spawn, delete the tree two ways, spawn again ->
restored on the same branch and HEAD); red before, green after.
